<title>JAPAN: Chuo Trust problem loans(Banking account).</title>
<headline>Chuo Trust problem loans(Banking account).</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chuo Trust &amp; Banking Co Ltd has disclosed its restructured loans (in billions of yen unless specified):</p>
<p>					end-Sep 96     end-Mar 96</p>
<p>  Restructured loans	     30.4	    110.1</p>
<p>  Bad loans			  50.1	     26.4</p>
<p>  Non-performing loans	   99.3	     94.0</p>
<p>  Loans to troubled clients	--		 --</p>
<p>  Total problem loans	   179.8	    230.5</p>
<p>Restructured loans are those on which interest rates have been cut to help corporate restructuring. Bad loans are to bankrupt firms and non-performing are those with interest payments in arrears by six months or more. Loans to troubled clients are mainly to the bank's non-bank affiliates.</p>
</text>
